@api @form_data
Feature: Valid Form Data Contract Tests # features/form_data.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the POST /post endpoint echoes form data correctly
  So that I can ensure form-data handling remains stable
  @api @form_data
  Feature: Valid Form Data Contract Tests  # features/form_data.feature:2

  @smoke @positive
  Scenario: Verify POST returns 200 with JSON content type          # features/form_data.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                            # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a POST request to "/post" with form data:           # features/steps/test_post_response_steps.py:15
      | key  | value |
      | foo1 | bar1  |
      | foo2 | bar2  |
    Then the response status code should be 200                     # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response Content-Type should contain "application/json" # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:64
    And the response should be a JSON object                        # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:77

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify form data fields are echoed in the form object  # features/form_data.feature:27
    Given the API base URL is configured                           # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a POST request to "/post" with form data:          # features/steps/test_post_response_steps.py:15
      | key  | value |
      | foo1 | bar1  |
      | foo2 | bar2  |
    Then the response status code should be 200                    # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the JSON key "form" should be of type "object"             # None
    And the JSON key "form.foo1" should equal "bar1"               # None
    And the JSON key "form.foo2" should equal "bar2"               # None

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify response contains all required contract keys  # features/form_data.feature:41
    Given the API base URL is configured                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a POST request to "/post" with form data:        # features/steps/test_post_response_steps.py:15
      | key  | value |
      | foo1 | bar1  |
      | foo2 | bar2  |
    Then the response should be a JSON object                    # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:77
    And the response JSON should contain key "form"              # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "headers"           # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "url"               # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82

  @contract @schema
  Scenario: Verify response matches the POST echo JSON schema  # features/form_data.feature:55
    Given the API base URL is configured                       # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a POST request to "/post" with form data:      # features/steps/test_post_response_steps.py:15
      | key  | value |
      | foo1 | bar1  |
      | foo2 | bar2  |
    Then the response status code should be 200                # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response should match the POST echo JSON schema    # features/steps/test_post_response_steps.py:33

  @performance @positive
  Scenario: Verify response time is within acceptable limits  # features/form_data.feature:67
    Given the API base URL is configured                      # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a POST request to "/post" with form data:     # features/steps/test_post_response_steps.py:15
      | key  | value |
      | foo1 | bar1  |
      | foo2 | bar2  |
    Then the response status code should be 200               # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response time should be under 5000 milliseconds   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:108

@api @query_params
Feature: Valid Query Params Contract Tests # features/query_params.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get endpoint echoes query parameters correctly
  So that I can ensure query param handling remains stable
  @api @query_params
  Feature: Valid Query Params Contract Tests  # features/query_params.feature:2

  @smoke @positive
  Scenario: Verify response returns 200 with correct Content-Type                # features/query_params.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:                   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response Content-Type should equal "application/json; charset=utf-8" # None

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify query parameters are correctly echoed in args  # features/query_params.feature:26
    Given the API base URL is configured                          # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:    # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the JSON key "args" should be of type "object"            # None
    And the JSON key "args.foo" should equal "bar"                # None
    And the JSON key "args.baz" should equal "value"              # None

  @contract @headers
  Scenario: Verify Date header exists and contains a valid date  # features/query_params.feature:40
    Given the API base URL is configured                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response should have header "Date"                   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:69
    And the response header "Date" should be a valid date        # None

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify response contains all required contract keys  # features/query_params.feature:53
    Given the API base URL is configured                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response should be a JSON object                    # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:77
    And the response JSON should contain key "args"              # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "headers"           # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "url"               # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify the url property contains the original request URL  # features/query_params.feature:67
    Given the API base URL is configured                               # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                        # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "postman-echo.com/get"       # None
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "foo=bar"                    # None
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "baz=value"                  # None

